== A. closed form (Prop 5.5) against brute force; K3 criteria
   optimal J agrees in 2100 / 2100 (population, lambda) cases (populations of 2-8 bodies, random parameters)
   cases with S the same with and without K3: 1473; K3 enters iff s|S| > L3: right in 1473; iff s|S| > lambda L3 (scout N2's statement): right in 1280
   counterexample: 15 bodies with 1000 observations, L=300, L3=150, k=60, s=15, c=12.4, lambda=2: J(law+K3+all) = 2250.0 < J(law+all) = 2400.0, so K3 enters; s|S| = 225 > L3 = 150, but s|S| < lambda L3 = 300

== B. Prop 5.6: 'lambda-MAP set constant on (tau, sigma)' <=> 'a vertex with sigma_{i+1} <= tau, sigma <= sigma_i'
   400 random point families x 10 random intervals: mismatches 0 / 4000 (MAP sets compared at every breakpoint inside the interval and between consecutive breakpoints)

