== E. Myrvold's unification term U(D1,D2;h) = I(h;D1 u D2) - I(h;D1) - I(h;D2), I(h;D) = log2 P_h(D)/P_0(D)
   model: each observation is one bit g(theta, t) of a fixed random table, c = 1 bit literal; parameters theta of k bits
   one body, stated parameter (deterministic theory): I(D1)=20.0 I(D2)=20.0 I(D1+D2)=40.0  U = 0.00
   one body, marginalised 6-bit parameter: I(D1)=14.00 I(D2)=14.00 I(D1+D2)=34.00  U = 6.00 (prediction: k = 6)
   two bodies, independent marginalised parameters: U = 0.00 (prediction 0)
   two bodies sharing a 3-bit universal constant (private 3 bits each): U = 3.00 (prediction 3)

